`ExtractedFact` in `types.ts` defines `value` as a `string`, not `boolean`:

```43:47:src/engine/types.ts
export interface ExtractedFact {
  category: BuildingFactCategory;
  key: string;
  value: string;
  confidenceScore: number;
}
```

The mock fact used `value: true`, which broke that contract. It’s now `value: "true"` so it matches `ExtractedFact` and the test still only cares that the extractor returns something (this run is about noisy scheduling metrics, not the fact payload). All seven tests in that file still pass.

